  "code": {
    "framework": "react",
    "package": "@coinbase/cds-web",
    "component": "Button",
    "import": "import { Button } from '@coinbase/cds-web/buttons';",
    "alwaysEmit": []
  },
  "notes": [
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "axes.state",
      "message": "A loading Button is also disabled (Pressable.tsx L225-L227), and :disabled sets pointer-events: none (Interactable.tsx L66-L71), so in use a loading Button is never hovered, pressed or focused. Those 48 tuples render as the cascade draws them when the State is forced (the pressed background and child opacity of [data-loading='true'] win, Pressable.tsx L48-L54). They stay in the selection; the owner can omit them in To-preview."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "axes.state",
      "message": "Active takes the :active and [aria-pressed='true'] rules (Interactable.tsx L57-L64). Pressable's scaledDownCss also scales the Button to 0.98 on :active (Pressable.tsx L30-L38); a Component Set variant has no transform, so the Active variant is drawn at full size."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "paint[state=focus].Button.stroke",
      "message": "The focus ring is a 2px solid outline in bgPrimary, 2px outside the border box (outline-offset, Interactable.tsx L80-L85). The Contract draws it as a 2px outside stroke with no gap. A spread drop shadow could keep the gap, but bgPrimary has no EFFECT_COLOR scope in the foundations document, so an effect cannot bind it (validation rule 6)."
    },
    {
      "level": "verify",
      "at": "paint[loading=on]",
      "message": "While loading, CDS centres an indeterminate ProgressCircle (24px, Button.tsx L27 and L327-L340) over the hidden label with position: absolute (spinnerContainerCss, L68-L76). The builder has no absolute children, so the loading variants show only the reserved label width and the icons at the pressed opacity. Compare a loading variant with the preview before approval."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "layout.Button.strokeWeight",
      "message": "Button passes borderWidth 0 (Button.tsx L231) with the variant's border colour, so no variant draws a border; stroke is none outside Focus. The variants' border tokens (button-<variant>-border) stay out of the closure."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "layout.Button.alignMain",
      "message": "With an icon, iconCss sets justify-content: space-between (Button.tsx L98-L100, L290), and the icon spans grow (flex-grow: 1, L82 and L92). A hugging Button has no free space, so space-between and center place the children alike; center matches the Button without icons (baseCss L51)."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "family",
      "message": "block (width 100%, Button.tsx L61-L66) and flush (a negative inline margin, L169-L173 and L266-L275) change how the Button sits in its parent, not how it draws, so they are not axes. compact is the deprecated alias of size s (dropped from size)."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "properties.startIcon",
      "message": "startIconActive and endIconActive (Button.tsx L161-L168) pick the active glyph of the same icon; the icon source uses the inactive glyphs only. start and end (L157-L164) take any React node instead of an icon name; the Contract models the icon names, which are the documented use (_webExamples.mdx L203-L232)."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "code",
      "message": "CDS's own Code Connect file (Button.figma.ts) maps five variants (no inverse, no deprecated foregroundMuted, L13-L19) and emits start/end nodes (L79-L80). The Contract follows Button.tsx: six variants, from ButtonBaseProps.ts, and the startIcon/endIcon names."
    }
  ],
